Z||000000||fropuff||07-14-2000||12:19 PM||||Hey, I was just wondering if anyone knows how to take out the molding clips.  It looks like you slip in a screwdriver and pry, but I'm not sure.  I don't really want to break the clips, but already broke three during removal, so it really doesn't matter.  Thanks.  ||||reg||10
Z||000001||TheFiero64||07-14-2000||07:37 PM||||You have to release them from behind the panel. You squeeze the tab in and it slides right out of the notch. They are too fragile <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I wonder if GM still stocks these?<P>------------------<BR>Joshua Bumpus<BR>New Bedford, MA<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fi.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||07-14-2000||08:53 PM||||Just break 'em off....easiest way. I did, then ordered a bunch through a Pontiac dealership here. They cost around 75 cents each...took a couple of days.||||reg||1
Z||000003||84 Indy||07-14-2000||08:54 PM||||Break them and buy new because most of them are gonna break any way.  The Fiero Store in Conn. has them i bought all new when i painted my car they were $15.00 to $20.00 for everything||||reg||6
